##  Taskbar cells, left to right.  Rendered by bin/mk-taskbar, which is called
##  from taskbar.proto (the QNX Photon restyle -- see that file for the
##  height/colorset/struts overrides it layers on top of config's own,
##  now-superseded FvwmTaskBar block).
##
##  Format:  <width>  <FvwmButtons button options>
##
##    <width>       cell width in pixels
##    flex          take an equal share of whatever pixels are left over
##    flex:N        take an N-times larger share than a plain flex cell
##    \             at end of line, continues onto the next
##
##  Everything after the width is passed through to FvwmButtons untouched, so
##  the full button syntax is available.  To add a launcher, add a line: the
##  flex cell shrinks to pay for it and the bar still spans the screen exactly.
##
##  Colorsets are named through infostore (cs_shelf / cs_shelf_hi / cs_shelf_well,
##  set up in shelf.proto) rather than raw numbers, so the taskbar and the
##  shelf can never drift into two different greys by accident.

##  Left: Launch.  Photon's own icon is a house/gear glyph; the closest
##  genuinely-16x16 file under images/icons is 16x16-wrench.png, a real
##  16x16 PNG made by pre-resizing the 18x18 wrench.png -- not FvwmButtons
##  scaling it at render time, which it cannot do anyway.
82   Icon "$[FVWM_ICON]/16x16-wrench.png", Title(Side,Left) "Launch", \
     Action(Mouse 1) Menu MenuFvwmRoot, Frame 0
6    Frame 0

##  Middle: window list.  FvwmIconMan is resized to whatever cell swallows it,
##  so this is the one cell that should absorb the slack.  Its own colours
##  (Photon grey, same 30/31 as everything else) are set on TaskBarIcons in
##  taskbar.proto, not here -- this cell just frames it.
flex Left, Swallow TaskBarIcons 'Module FvwmIconMan TaskBarIcons', Frame 0

##  Right: tray, volume, clock
6    Frame 0
##  10 slots of 26px, matching max_geometry/slot_size in stalonetrayrc after
##  its Photon-height shrink.  The tray never shrinks (no_shrink), so the
##  cell has to fit it at full size.
260  Swallow(NoClose,UseOld) stalonetray \
     `Exec exec stalonetray --config "$[FVWM_USERDIR]/stalonetrayrc"`, \
     Frame 0
6    Frame 0
50   Title "VOL", Action(Mouse 1) Exec exec pavucontrol, \
     Action(Mouse 4) Exec exec wpctl set-volume @DEFAULT_SINK@ 5%+, \
     Action(Mouse 5) Exec exec wpctl set-volume @DEFAULT_SINK@ 5%-, \
     Frame 0
6    Frame 0
##  Clock: a plain button, not a Swallow.  Its text is pushed in from outside
##  by TaskbarClockTick in taskbar.proto (SendToModule ... ChangeButton),
##  which is what lets it read as one sunken field, "Fri-19 11:33PM" -- the
##  swallowed FvwmScript-DateTime this replaced drew its own two-line HH:MM /
##  date pair inside its own window chrome, which does not sit flush the way
##  Photon's single field does.  Id names it for ChangeButton to find; the
##  starting empty Title is filled within a few hundred ms of the module
##  coming up, see the Schedule calls at the end of taskbar.proto.
120  Id TaskbarClock, Title "", Frame -1, Colorset $[infostore.cs_shelf_well]
6    Frame 0
